WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.490
Film Courage: I believe you’re a fan of
Walter White of Breaking Bad?

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.509
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau: Yes.

00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:05.879
Most of us are.

00:00:05.879 --> 00:00:06.899
Film Courage: Yes!

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:10.730
Were you thinking of his character when you
were preparing to play Jacob (“Money”)

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:11.730
in SHOT CALLER?

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.840
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau: No…I mean I love
Breaking Bad.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.100
I was a huge fan.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.910
There are definitely similarities.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.390
I mean he is a regular guy suddenly turning
to crime.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.179
I think there is a difference though.

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:32.770
Walter White made a choice.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:38.660
Well of course Jacob makes choices but they
are pretty much forced on him so I think that

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.650
is a significant difference.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:46.010
Film Courage: Let’s pretend we have a time
machine and we go back to 1993/1994.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.010
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau: Okay.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:48.180
Film Courage: The film NIGHTWATCH?

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.180
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau: Yes.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:52.670
Film Courage: So let’s say we wrapped on
the film.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:56.370
Did you have a Plan B just in case this crazy
acting thing didn’t work out?

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.370
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau: Oh, no!

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:01.440
Never had a Plan B for some reason…very
stupid.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:12.700
I’ve always had a very (I guess) unrealistic
belief that it would work out but it did for

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.700
some reason.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:14.700
Yeah…

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.160
Film Courage: Do you think that there was
a strategy to it, besides your talent?

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:25.900
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau: No…I wanted to…I
had a dream even when I did NIGHTWATCH, I

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:30.850
had already been accepted to a theater school
in England.

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:34.250
So I just finished four years of training
in Denmark and then I was going to do this

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:38.170
movie and then go to Bristol Old Vic (theatre
school), where Daniel Day-Lewis had gone (it

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.170
was very exciting).

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:42.240
I went there for two weeks and then I ran
away.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:48.170
But I always wanted to act and I wanted to
travel the world (if I could).

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.170
So that was the plan.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:53.050
Then I moved to London and then slowly but
surely I started getting work.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:58.950
Film Courage: Now you’re in a similar boat
soon with Game of Thrones if it ends.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:03.700
Does it put new pressure on you to find something
or you feel it’s almost like freedom?

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.440
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau: Well it’s not like
it just happened.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.490
I mean I’ve been doing this for 25 years.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.340
I’ve been working every year.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.300
I haven’t had any downtime.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:18.130
I mean to worry that you’re in something
that is successful that’s going to hurt

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.130
you.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:20.170
That is the least of my worries.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:21.640
It’s usually the other way around.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:26.030
You do something and you worry that no one
will want to see it.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:32.351
And I’ve been working every year doing Game
of Thrones and I hope that if I choose, I

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:33.410
would continue to be working.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.080
Film Courage: Do you like the unknown?

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.860
The freedom of possibility?

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:43.870
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau: Yeah…I mean that’s
I guess the nature of being an actor unless

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:50.590
you are in a theater but usually most actors,
we are all freelance and it’s not so much

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.010
a question of liking it, it’s just the way
it is.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:54.630
Film Courage: Thank you!

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:55.849
Nikolaj Coster-Waldau: Yes.

00:02:55.849 --> 00:02:56.659
Thank you!

